WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.327 --> 00:00:19.570
the king and the duke had fallen asleep in the hut on the raft, Jim said to me,

2
00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:22.492
"Do you think the duke and the king are rascals?"

3
00:00:23.593 --> 00:00:25.454
"Yes, I do," I replied.

4
00:00:25.474 --> 00:00:29.317
"From the books I've read, I've learned that many kings are rascals."

5
00:00:29.337 --> 00:00:33.760
"Then I hope we don't meet any more of them," said Jim.

6
00:00:34.636 --> 00:00:36.537
"These two are all I can stand."

7
00:00:38.419 --> 00:00:40.640
I went to sleep while Jim kept watch.

8
00:00:41.461 --> 00:00:46.244
He was supposed to wake me later so that I could take my turn to watch, but he

9
00:00:46.284 --> 00:00:46.904
let me sleep.

10
00:00:47.725 --> 00:00:49.106
When I awoke, it was dawn.

11
00:00:50.527 --> 00:00:54.970
I saw Jim sitting with his head bent low, and I knew he was feeling sad.

12
00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:58.512
I asked him if he was thinking about his wife and children.

13
00:00:59.913 --> 00:01:02.174
"Yes, I am," he replied.

14
00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:04.156
"I miss them so much.

15
00:01:04.828 --> 00:01:08.709
I'm afraid I'll never see my little Elizabeth and my little Johnny again."

16
00:01:09.489 --> 00:01:10.550
I tried to comfort him.

17
00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:14.911
I was thinking that black slaves had all the same feelings as white people.

18
00:01:16.071 --> 00:01:17.892
They loved their families just as much.

19
00:01:19.032 --> 00:01:23.594
I began to wonder how anyone could sell a man and separate him from his family.

20
00:01:25.634 --> 00:01:30.656
The king and the duke wished they could stage the Royal Nonesuch again because they had made so

21
00:01:30.696 --> 00:01:31.136
much money.

22
00:01:32.348 --> 00:01:36.072
But they were afraid news of their trick might have spread to other towns.

23
00:01:36.973 --> 00:01:39.595
If it had, they would need to think of a new scam.

24
00:01:41.357 --> 00:01:45.541
Meanwhile, they bought themselves fine new clothes at the next town we came to.

25
00:01:46.442 --> 00:01:48.624
They even bought some new clean clothes for me.

26
00:01:49.845 --> 00:01:55.650
They told me that it was easier to fool people if you looked rich and respectable, and they

27
00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:57.032
proved this to me the next day.

28
00:01:58.324 --> 00:02:02.968
The king and the duke asked me to take them in our canoe to the nearest steamboat wharf.

29
00:02:04.029 --> 00:02:05.970
There we could board a big steamboat.

30
00:02:07.331 --> 00:02:11.174
Then they could arrive at the next town as if they were very important people.

31
00:02:12.155 --> 00:02:15.317
They said that I could pretend to be their servant, Adolphus.

32
00:02:16.378 --> 00:02:20.862
I didn't like that name, but I was so excited to be riding on a steamboat for the

33
00:02:20.922 --> 00:02:23.364
first time in my life that I didn't object.

34
00:02:24.804 --> 00:02:30.527
As we boarded the steamboat, the king started a conversation with a friendly and trusting young man.

35
00:02:30.547 --> 00:02:34.409
"When I first saw you, I thought you might be Mr.

36
00:02:34.449 --> 00:02:36.750
Harvey Wilks," the young man said.

37
00:02:37.751 --> 00:02:43.294
The king replied, "No, I am Alexander Blodgett—but who is Mr.

38
00:02:43.354 --> 00:02:52.579
Wilks?" "Well, everyone in our town has been waiting for Harvey Wilks and his brother William—William can't hear

39
00:02:52.659 --> 00:02:54.440
or speak—to arrive from England.

40
00:02:55.544 --> 00:02:58.525
They are coming to see their brother Peter, who lived in our town.

41
00:02:59.625 --> 00:03:05.287
When Peter fell very ill a month ago, he wrote to them asking them to come, but I'm

42
00:03:05.327 --> 00:03:07.207
afraid Peter passed away yesterday."

43
00:03:07.227 --> 00:03:11.048
"Didn't Peter have any other relatives?"

44
00:03:11.729 --> 00:03:12.269
asked the king.

45
00:03:13.129 --> 00:03:15.450
"He did have a brother George, who lived nearby.

46
00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:20.291
But George and his wife both died a few months ago, leaving three daughters."

47
00:03:21.391 --> 00:03:23.112
Then the young man's face brightened.

48
00:03:24.076 --> 00:03:26.437
"But at least Peter left a letter for Harvey.

49
00:03:27.818 --> 00:03:31.520
People in town say that the letter tells Harvey where Peter hid all his money.

50
00:03:32.521 --> 00:03:37.503
Peter wanted to be sure that Harvey would share the money with George's three daughters because their father

51
00:03:37.543 --> 00:03:38.404
was a poor man."

52
00:03:39.564 --> 00:03:42.386
"Why, what are the dear girls' names?"

53
00:03:43.026 --> 00:03:44.067
asked the king keenly.

54
00:03:45.207 --> 00:03:47.529
"Mary Jane is the oldest—she's 19.

55
00:03:48.069 --> 00:03:50.991
Then there's Susan, who is 15, and Joanna, 14."

56
00:03:52.071 --> 00:03:58.616
The king shook his head at the sadness of their young lives, and then continued his questioning: "Was

57
00:03:58.696 --> 00:04:00.518
Peter Wilks a wealthy man?"

58
00:04:00.538 --> 00:04:04.941
"Oh, yes," replied the young man innocently.

59
00:04:04.961 --> 00:04:07.704
"He owned several houses and land.

60
00:04:08.744 --> 00:04:12.227
People say he had three or four thousand dollars hidden away somewhere."

61
00:04:12.247 --> 00:04:16.651
"Have Harvey and William Wilks ever come to visit before?"

62
00:04:16.671 --> 00:04:19.393
"No," said the young man.

63
00:04:19.413 --> 00:04:22.696
"Everyone in town is very curious to meet them."

64
00:04:25.484 --> 00:04:30.347
By the time we got off that steamboat, the king had found out everything there was to know

65
00:04:30.467 --> 00:04:31.448
about Peter Wilks.

66
00:04:32.769 --> 00:04:37.772
The friendly young man was continuing south to New Orleans where he would board a ship to South

67
00:04:37.812 --> 00:04:43.096
America. So there was no one to stop the king and the duke from pretending to be Harvey

68
00:04:43.256 --> 00:04:44.056
and William Wilks.

69
00:04:45.017 --> 00:04:46.478
And that is just what they did.

70
00:04:48.359 --> 00:04:52.082
The king and the duke walked from the steamboat wharf into the town.

71
00:04:52.942 --> 00:04:55.184
I followed them, carrying their suitcases.

72
00:04:56.336 --> 00:04:59.857
There they met some men who had gathered to watch the steamboat arrive.

73
00:05:00.937 --> 00:05:05.238
The king asked anxiously, "Can anyone tell me where Mr.

74
00:05:05.378 --> 00:05:06.699
Peter Wilks lives?"

75
00:05:06.719 --> 00:05:11.220
"I'm very sorry, sir," said one of the men.

76
00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:13.241
"Peter Wilks has died."

77
00:05:14.641 --> 00:05:18.942
The king grabbed the man and sobbed on his shoulder, "Oh no!

78
00:05:19.422 --> 00:05:20.863
Our poor brother!"

79
00:05:28.782 --> 00:05:30.403
Then the duke started crying too.

80
00:05:31.784 --> 00:05:35.086
The townspeople gathered around and said how sorry they were.

81
00:05:36.847 --> 00:05:40.730
Then they led us to a house where three girls were standing in a doorway.

82
00:05:42.271 --> 00:05:47.094
The oldest girl—I knew she must be Mary Jane—was red-haired and beautiful.

83
00:05:48.415 --> 00:05:51.717
She ran to hug the king, who she thought was her uncle Harvey.

84
00:05:52.778 --> 00:05:57.559
The other two girls cried and hugged the duke, who they thought was their deaf uncle William.

85
00:05:58.561 --> 00:06:02.908
I felt ashamed of these two liars and ashamed of myself for being with them.
